body:
@bruvzg I'm sorry but I think #106783 was a mistake. AccessKit already guarantee that the accessibility tree will only be initialized if an assistive technology is running. Furthermore, why would this crash occur only after an action in the UI? I will take the blame for the unhelpful error messages.

If you can reproduce this yourself, could you please do it with a debug version of the C bindings so we get nicer stack traces? I can see a few places that could generate this error.

I will try to squeeze better error reporting in the next version or so.
